## Design-gap notes (reported, not invented)

- The shared `yang.call` module tree ([yang/core/call.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc1/src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:168)) is not annotated: it is shared with the ts/php/py tracks, and the brief's track isolation forbids touching it this round. Clojure linked programs pin that module, so its own occurrences await the shared adoption; the clojure-emitted preamble around it is covered.
- The relay thread's dynamic-call-site edge (`$$`, `extract`, eval) is covered by the design as written: the marker carries no callee identity, so a runtime-computed callee needs no "dynamic" mark — the lexically fixed application occurrence gets its K (§2.1 statically-indirect coverage, §7 indirect gate). Eval-admitted code is a separate admission whose origin the admitting composition supplies; no lexical site is fabricated for it.
- `publish-module!` still publishes rows only; persisting C1 side tables beside manifests is D1 durable-correspondence work, out of round 1 scope. Markers reach consumers today through the encoder side table.

Suite-scale commands for the seat (jupiter), per the brief's test-boundary ruling: `clojure -M:test` (full JVM), `bb test:cljs`, `bb test:cljd`, and the jolt core lane `bb test:jolt-core` — the generated-parser namespaces must be built first (`clj -M:antlr-gen`) for the catalog/cross-language suites to load.
